rem An Enormous Factorial
rem https://projecteuler.net/problem=288
rem Count the factors p in the factorial
rem of N = sum of T[n] p^n, n up to Q,
rem with T[n] = S[n] mod p, S[n+1] =
rem S[n]^2 mod 50515093, S[0] = 290797,
rem modulo p^Exp

use numbers
use io
use cli

option P integer = 61
option Q integer = 10000000
option Exp integer = 10

rem By Legendre the count is
rem (N - s) / (p - 1) with s the digit
rem sum of N in base p: the T[n] are the
rem digits. Take N modulo M =
rem (p - 1) p^Exp. As p^n = p^Exp mod M
rem from n = Exp on, the tail of T only
rem enters as its sum.
Mod = (P - 1) * P ** Exp
S = 290797
Low = 0
Tail = 0
Total = 0
Pw = 1
for K in 0 to Q
  T = S mod P
  Total += T
  if K less Exp
    Low += T * Pw
    Pw *= P
  else
    Tail += T
  end
  S = S * S mod 50515093
end
Rest = Low + Tail * P ** Exp
Count = (Rest - Total) // (P - 1)
Answer = Count mod (P ** Exp)
Answer print
